    "finding": "At 320 turns, the relay's peak context is FLAT across the sweep (120000 tokens, 60% of the window — out of the context-rot zone), while compaction peaks at 192571 (96% — pinned at the wall). The relay bills 4113600 effective tokens vs compaction's 6926106 (59% of the cost), force-rewrites only 96000 cache-busted tokens vs compaction's 846893 (11% — it resets an O(1) baton, not a near-wall prefix), and retains 100% of load-bearing facts vs 36%. Raw cache-hit rate is comparable (0.90 vs 0.93; compaction's is marginally higher only because it runs a larger resident prefix). Peak, cost, cache-preservation, and fidelity favor the relay; the comparison is a hermetic model, so the numbers are the SIGN, not a provider-billed total."
